From: Mixtile <support@mixtile.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: blade3: raise TYPEC1 sink capability to 20V/3A

TYPEC1 is the board's DC input. Its VBUS is the only path into the
VCC12V~20V_DCIN rail, through a 30V/4A MOSFET and a 24V/3A fuse, and the
power tree specifies 20V at 3A for it.

The connector description asks for 1A on every sink PDO, and tcpm clamps
its request at min(source PDO, sink PDO), so the board settles on 20V/1A --
20W on a rail specified for 60W. Raise both sink PDOs to 3000mA.

op-sink-microwatt stays at 15W. The binding defines it as the required
operating power, not the maximum input rating, and it does not cap the
negotiated current; it is also the value the U-Boot board description uses.

Drop the PPS APDO: the board's input is a fixed 12-20V rail with no
programmable-voltage path.

power-role and data-role are left alone -- the port is still used for USB
host and DP Alt Mode.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-mixtile-blade3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-mixtile-blade3.dts
index 67402ad..77c208f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-mixtile-blade3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588-mixtile-blade3.dts
@@ -790,9 +790,8 @@
 			faster-pd-negotiation;
 			op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
 			sink-pdos =
-				<PDO_FIXED(5000, 1000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)
-				PDO_VAR(5000, 20000, 1000)
-				PDO_PPS_APDO(5000, 20000, 1000)>;
+				<PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)
+				PDO_VAR(5000, 20000, 3000)>;
 			source-pdos =
 				<PDO_FIXED(5000, 1000, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
 
